## Figure S-common caption DRAFT

> Figure S-common | Saved exploratory PR costs relative to the best deterministic PF in the registered common domain. The three panels show H2/H4/H6 under the common conditions specified in Supplementary Section S-common-1 (linear 1 Å, STO-3G, tol-only DF1e-8 ranks 3/10/19, T = 0.8, P = 0, prefixes 0–2/1–9/5–15 plus Full3/10/19, q = 1/2/4/8, δ = 0.8/0.4/0.2/0.1). Each point uses the saved PR_reduction_percent field from the all-formula comparison. Positive values denote lower PR point cost and negative values lower PF point cost. Accuracies are categorical and are not interpolated. Candidate identities and unchanged PR statistics are provided in Table S-common-B. No new ratios, rankings or uncertainty intervals are calculated for this proposal. These finite selected point costs do not certify population-mean superiority or rigorous bias; unobserved rare-event contributions remain unknown. The H6 interrupted-stage provenance is retained as described in Section S-common-5.

